# nr-office-ooxml-docx-revisions: integration fragment

Three modules of the crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml, created by nr-office-ooxml-package): docx_revisions
(the tracked-change tree and the redlining audit, lint and accept/reject of docx-revisions.mjs), validation_package (the
package validation of portable-validation-package.mjs, with the saxes 6 / jsdom well-formedness check of every XML part
written out rule by rule) and chart_faults (portable-chart-faults.mjs). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name
belongs to them.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

lib.rs belongs to nr-office-ooxml-package; the three module lines are written here so the lead applies them with the other
tasks' lines of the wave. In the module list, in alphabetical place:

    pub mod chart_faults;       (after `pub mod cells;`)
    pub mod docx_revisions;     (after `pub mod chart_faults;`)
    pub mod validation_package; (after `pub mod template_tokens;`, before `pub mod xml;`)

and in the module doc's "This part:" list, after "the document fingerprint ([`fingerprint`])", add:
", the tracked changes of a Word part ([`docx_revisions`]), the package validation ([`validation_package`]) and the chart
faults of a deck ([`chart_faults`])".

## native/core/Cargo.toml, native/core/Cargo.lock, crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml

No change: the modules use only dependencies the crate already lists (mixdog-fsio for the read proof, mixdog-js, serde_json,
sha2; dev: tempfile, and mixdog-office-base with feature test-support for the twin test). No new crate.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-detect and before office-engine (the list is sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-revisions.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-docx-revisions/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "c4316253c5a83762c8ccbea8bc221009c9669054d2a347288fe70602fb1439a4",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-revisions.mjs",
      "set": "office-docx-revisions",
      "totalBytes": 319133
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-docx-revisions/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool
that keeps this file reorders or reformats them.)

## What the twin test needs

tests/twin_docx_revisions.rs replays native/core/fixtures/office-docx-revisions/golden.json without Node: 115 function
cases (docx-revisions and portable-chart-faults), 38 packages (validatePortableOoxml: valid, missing parts, broken
relationships, 115 malformed-XML parts with jsdom's messages, tracked changes, redlining against a source, protected parts,
presentation faults) and 2 chart scans. twin_live_docx_revisions (ignored) re-records through Node.

## Compiled outside the workspace

The wave is compiled by the lead; cargo was not run. The three modules, the twin test and every unit test were compiled and
run with plain rustc against the real crates regress 0.10.5 and serde_json 1.0.149 (preserve_order) and against stand-ins for
the parts of mixdog-js, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-ooxml (zip container, opc) and mixdog-office-base they call: 47 unit tests and the
twin replay passed. What that did not exercise: the real JsRegex wrapper (its pre-filter and identity-escape pass over the
same patterns), the real zip container (entry order and DOS dates) and the real twin normaliser. The first cargo test of
mixdog-ooxml is the check for those.
